 "notes": [
  "Display timing, useful on a scope: 262 horizontal lines per frame, each line 768 clocks of the 12 MHz base, repeating 60 times a second. The 12.096 MHz oscillator is crystal Y1 with transistor Q9 and discretes rather than a packaged part.",
  "Sync chain: P4/P5/P6 divide 12 MHz down to 1H-256H; 256H inverted clocks the vertical counters N6/N5 for 1V-128V; those address sync PROM M6 whose output is latched by L6. A blank screen with a good 12 MHz at Y1 points down this chain."
